{"id": "EUVD-2026-45839", "enisaUuid": "395dace2-a3dd-3532-87d9-a9b96287994f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/msm/adreno: Fix a reference leak in a6xx_gpu_init()\n\nIn a6xx_gpu_init(), node is obtained via of_parse_phandle().\nWhile there was a manual of_node_put() at the end of the\ncommon path, several early error returns would bypass this call,\nresulting in a reference leak.\nFix this by using the __free(device_node) cleanup handler to\nrelease the reference when the variable goes out of scope.\n\nPatchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/700661/", "datePublished": "2026-07-19T15:40:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:43:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bdad77438cc2ba006b041eb02adccb0b9f8cffad", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bd750e4043bbd9e2ef69de50b11bd6f98c366cc0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b76568c6721840a4ddb65e24e2849db0f8e83461", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2be24c945e76cd538ce5dd2e50f5d3e7d848c175", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e64bca63647db1d5518198d6c5ca2dbcc66b182b"], "aliases": ["GHSA-cf8p-8jpf-qj34", "CVE-2026-64154"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "027971b6-171b-321b-ba9f-267167dd2c7c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a903a44a98471cedf0021fac0a6a64bbe86943f <b76568c6721840a4ddb65e24e2849db0f8e83461"}, {"id": "02c2a06f-d82a-3809-b3de-8edef009d033", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "053ed293-8fbe-31ef-8e42-7bedb6175197", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a903a44a98471cedf0021fac0a6a64bbe86943f <bdad77438cc2ba006b041eb02adccb0b9f8cffad"}, {"id": "23a473c7-c60f-3a94-8374-861d7a202b43", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "8441ed01-f835-3d95-a88a-c05403daaf79", "product": {"